# COURSE_ID exercise thoughts

> A lazy carrier: created from the template only when a student thought really arises out of answering an
> exercise; never pre-created as an empty file.
> This file summarizes those thoughts for later exercises, retests and method transfer to read.
> It is not a second source of truth for the original answer or the student's words; the student's words
> are governed by the linked Attempt.
> The deduplication key is the `Unit / Attempt / Problem` source tuple; a full answer is never copied.
> The rules are in `main/50_playbook/exercise_evidence.md` §3.

## Entry format

```markdown
## UNIT_ID / ATdddd / PROBLEM_ID / YYYY-MM-DD

- Source: [ATdddd](exerciseNN/attempts/ATdddd/attempt.md)
- Short excerpt of the student's words: a directly quotable, traceable quotation, not rewritten
- Teacher distillation: a model paraphrase may only go in this column and must never mix into the words above
- Index tags: tag, tag
- Later use: how to use this the next time a problem of the same kind comes up
- Reasoning pattern: not promoted / promoted to reasoning_patterns.md (requires repeating across at least two problems, with transfer)
- Course distillation: REFL-COURSE_ID-dddd or —
```

